#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1097 expect=violation domain=SUPPAE1
#note "PLAN-split-supp-resolution (Q1, D7): the split SUPPAE family (SUPPAE1 + SUPPAE2, RDOMAIN=AE) resolves to the union of both members, and record_count's filter=(QNAM == \"AETRTEM\") is applied OVER THAT UNION: neither member carries AETRTEM, the filtered count is 0 and the dataset-level violation fires on the SUPPAE1 primary. Pins the filter= regression on a family union (an unfiltered or mis-filtered count over 2 rows would be 2 and silence the rule). Green on the pre-plan engine too (the family resolved to nothing, count 0) -- the valid twin is the red-first witness."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset SUPPAE1 label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE (part 1)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP | Other Medically Important SAE | N
---

dataset SUPPAE2 label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE (part 2)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | AE | 002 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP | Other Medically Important SAE | Y
---
